// Golden fixture: a REAL gcc-produced ELF64 relocatable object carrying a
// BAKED, RELOCATION-LESS intra-`.text` call --
// D-LK-STATIC-LINK-INTRASECTION-BAKED-CALL. Embedded byte-for-byte so the
// guard is deterministic and CI-portable (no gcc at test time).
//
// ★★★ BUILT WITH NOTHING BUT `gcc -O2 -c`. No `-ffunction-sections` (that is
// gcc's DEFAULT), no `-falign-functions`, no flags of any kind beyond the
// optimisation level every distro static library is built with. gcc 13.3.0,
// x86_64. This matters because the deferral this fixture closes assumed the
// shape needed an unusual build; ✔MEASURED, `-O2` and `-O3` both produce it.
//
// SHAPE -- one `.text`, THREE `STT_FUNC` symbols, and NO `.rela.text` at all:
//
//     helper   @ 0x00, size  4   (LOCAL, static)
//     filler   @ 0x10, size  9   (LOCAL, static, unreferenced)
//     compute  @ 0x20, size 13   (GLOBAL)
//
// The offsets are 16-byte aligned, so the section carries 12 and 7 bytes of
// INTER-FUNCTION PADDING that belongs to no symbol -- `st_size` covers the
// body only. `compute` calls `helper` as `E8 D7 FF FF FF`, a rel32 of -41
// resolved by the ASSEMBLER, with no relocation to repair it.
//
// ⚠ WHY THIS IS A SILENT WRONG-CODE WITNESS AND NOT A LINK ERROR. DSS
// reconstructs each `STT_FUNC` as its own atom and re-lays them out packed,
// dropping the padding that belonged to no atom. ✔MEASURED end-to-end before
// the fix: DSS linked it with rc 0 and ZERO diagnostics, the baked call
// resolved to `main+0x7`, and the binary SEGFAULTED (exit 139) where the
// native gcc link of the same two objects exits 42.

